title: Law and Order
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/law_order.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and law_order_timer <= 0
on-arrival: law_order_timer = 6; month_actions += 1

= Law and Order

Willie Whitelaw at the Home Office has a full in-tray.

- @police_pay: Implement the Edmund-Davies police pay award in full.
- @short_sharp_shock: A "short, sharp shock" for young offenders.
- @hanging: Allow a free vote on restoring the death penalty.
- @scarman: Implement the Scarman Report.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@police_pay
view-if: police_pay_done = 0
subtitle: -1 budget.
on-arrival: police_pay_done = 1; budget -= 1; right_dissent -= 4; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent)

Police pay rises by up to 45%. Recruitment picks up, and the Police Federation is delighted.

@short_sharp_shock
on-arrival: right_dissent -= 3; c1_lib += 1; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent)

Military-style detention centres for young offenders. The party conference cheers; criminologists doubt it will work.

@hanging
view-if: hanging_vote = 0
subtitle: Popular in the country and on the right. The House will almost certainly vote it down.
on-arrival: hanging_vote = 1; right_dissent -= 4; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent += 2; lib_relation -= 3
achievement: hanging

You have always believed in capital punishment for the worst murders, and you say so. In a free vote, the Commons rejects restoring the death penalty by 362 votes to 243, with Whitelaw and most of the Cabinet in the majority. The polls say three-quarters of the public wanted it back.

@scarman
view-if: riots >= 1 and scarman_done = 0
subtitle: The wets approve; the right says it rewards rioters.
on-arrival: scarman_done = 1; wet_dissent -= 4; right_dissent += 3; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); budget -= 1
achievement: scarman

Lord Scarman's report on Brixton calls for community policing, better recruitment from ethnic minorities, and an end to stop-and-search under the "sus" law.
